Setting a key rewrites every non-ASCII value in the fence as an escape
sequence. `--set "title=Café"` writes `title: "Caf\xE9"`.

Frontmatter.serializeYAML calls Yams.dump without allowUnicode, and
that parameter defaults to false, which tells libyaml to escape every
character outside ASCII.

This is the same defect as in frontmatter-reads-a-value-holding-non-
ascii-text, but on the write path, where it costs the user more: with
-i the escaped bytes land in the file. Setting one unrelated key is
enough to rewrite every accented word, dash and CJK character in a
fence the user typed by hand.

Yams.dump should be called with allowUnicode: true.
